Define the vector arithmetic and comparison operators for half in the C++ prelude.

The C++ target emits half vectors as Vector<half, N> and their arithmetic and comparisons as the
ordinary operators. prelude/slang-cpp-types-core.h instantiates SLANG_FLOAT_VECTOR_OPS, which
defines + - * / unary - and the six comparisons for a vector element type, for float and double
(lines 371-372) and not for half. Slang's own tests/compute/half-vector-calc.slang and
half-vector-compare.slang therefore emit C++ that does not compile against the prelude: clang
22.1.8, "invalid operands to binary expression ('Vector<half, 3>' (aka 'Vector<_Float16, 3>') and
'Vector<half, 3>')".

This instantiates SLANG_FLOAT_VECTOR_OPS(half) beside the other two where half is declared.
slang-cpp-scalar-intrinsics.h declares it, and slang-cpp-prelude.h includes it before the types; it
now also defines SLANG_PRELUDE_HAS_HALF, which slang-cpp-types-core.h tests. A host that includes
the types alone, as slang-rhi's CPU backend includes slang-cpp-types.h, has no half and gets no
operators for it.

Measured on v2026.21 (win-x64): both tests' C++ output refused by clang++ -std=c++17
-fsyntax-only with the prelude at the tag on the include path. An unconditional instantiation broke
slang-rhi's CPU backend in a build with SLANG_ENABLE_TESTS (MSVC C2065, 'half': undeclared
identifier).
diff --git a/prelude/slang-cpp-scalar-intrinsics.h b/prelude/slang-cpp-scalar-intrinsics.h
index c13763c..16f90c6 100644
--- a/prelude/slang-cpp-scalar-intrinsics.h
+++ b/prelude/slang-cpp-scalar-intrinsics.h
@@ -741,6 +741,10 @@ struct half
 };
 #endif
 
+// `half` is declared above. slang-cpp-types-core.h, when included after this header, defines the
+// vector operators for it.
+#define SLANG_PRELUDE_HAS_HALF 1
+
 half U16_ashalf(uint16_t x);
 
 union Union16
diff --git a/prelude/slang-cpp-types-core.h b/prelude/slang-cpp-types-core.h
index 10d694b..b1e45e4 100644
--- a/prelude/slang-cpp-types-core.h
+++ b/prelude/slang-cpp-types-core.h
@@ -370,6 +370,11 @@ SLANG_INT_VECTOR_OPS(uintptr_t)
 
 SLANG_FLOAT_VECTOR_OPS(float)
 SLANG_FLOAT_VECTOR_OPS(double)
+// `half` exists only where slang-cpp-scalar-intrinsics.h was included first, as the C++ prelude
+// does; a host including the types alone has no `half` and no operators for it.
+#ifdef SLANG_PRELUDE_HAS_HALF
+SLANG_FLOAT_VECTOR_OPS(half)
+#endif
 
 #define SLANG_VECTOR_INT_NEG_OP(T)                      \
     template<int N>                                     \
